{"kind": "mod", "id": 820, "name": "Door Randomizer", "slug": "door-randomizer", "teaser": "Getting tired of doors always being in the same state at raid start? Randomize them instead!", "owner_name": "DrakiaXYZ", "downloads": 45466, "favourites": 35, "featured": false, "contains_ads": false, "contains_ai_content": false, "cheat_notice": false, "license_name": "MIT License", "guid": "xyz.drakia.doorrandomizer", "thumbnail_local": "thumbs/1107.png", "category": "Other", "category_id": 17, "updated_at": "2026-08-03T06:02:26.000000Z", "created_at": "2023-03-30T17:30:04.000000Z", "published_at": "2023-03-30T17:30:00.000000Z", "latest_constraint": "~4.1.0", "latest_version": "1.8.0", "has_local": false, "has_github": false, "license_link": "https://choosealicense.com/licenses/mit/", "description_html": "<p>Super simple client mod that will randomize the open state of every non-locked door on raid start.</p>\n<p>At the start of every raid, for each compatible door on the map, there is a 50% chance it will be swapped to its non-initial state.</p>\n<h3>Install Instructions</h3>\n<p>1) Open the downloaded zip file in 7-zip</p>\n<p>2) Select the folders in the zip file in 7-zip</p>\n<p>3) Drag the selected folders from 7-zip into your SPT folder</p>\n<p>Demonstration Video (Yes, it’s Quest Tracker, but the same concept applies to all of my mods, I’m not making mod-specific extraction example videos):</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/afNPjAw.gif\" alt=\"Install Gif\" /></p>\n<p>If you enjoy my work, you can <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://ko-fi.com/drakiaxyz\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">feed my caffeine addiction</a></p>\n<p><strong>NOTE: Any requests for assistance MUST be accompanied by the “BepInEx/LogOutput.log” file. Any support request without this file provided will be met with a request for this file, then ignored. Log content can be uploaded to: <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"h